---
import ProjectList from '@/components/content/ProjectList.astro';
import Section from '@/components/ui/Section.astro';
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { getPublishedProjects } from '@/lib/content';

const projects = await getPublishedProjects();
---

<PageLayout section="projects">
  <Section id="approach" label="Approach" title="Public work, with its source.">
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-lede text-ink-muted">
      <p>
        The path is how the mechanisms are taught. These are public repositories that use some of
        them, not case studies of employer systems. Each entry states the problem the repository
        takes on, the approach that is actually in the code, the techniques it uses, and what the
        repository demonstrates. A demonstration is not a measured result. Where the repository
        does not report a number, this page does not supply one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Status is part of the reading. Shipped means finished and usable. Archived means kept so
        the pipeline can be reread, not maintained. Employer work — the systems behind a job — lives
        on the résumé, where the context is the role rather than a repository.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="index" label="Index" title="Selected projects">
    <ProjectList projects={projects} />
  </Section>
</PageLayout>
